{"type":"standard","title":"Gus Bilirakis","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Gus Bilirakis</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q1555314","titles":{"canonical":"Gus_Bilirakis","normalized":"Gus Bilirakis","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Gus Bilirakis</span></span>"},"pageid":5648306,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Gus_Bilirakis%2C_official_portrait%2C_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Gus_Bilirakis%2C_official_portrait%2C_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":422},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0b/Gus_Bilirakis%2C_official_portrait%2C_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":565,"height":722},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1363404667","tid":"ff8f972b-7bf5-11f1-9cc9-c921b2401971","timestamp":"2026-07-10T00:26:31Z","description":"American politician & lawyer (born 1963)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gus_Bilirakis","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gus_Bilirakis?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gus_Bilirakis?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Gus_Bilirakis"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gus_Bilirakis","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Gus_Bilirakis","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gus_Bilirakis?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Gus_Bilirakis"}},"extract":"Gus Michael Bilirakis is an American lawyer and politician serving as the U.S. representative for Florida's 12th congressional district since 2013. A member of the Republican Party, he first entered Congress in 2007, where he succeeded his father Michael Bilirakis, representing Florida's 9th congressional district until redistricting. His district includes much of the northern portion of the Tampa Bay area. Bilirakis previously served as the Florida state representative for the 48th district from 1998 to 2006.","extract_html":"<p><b>Gus Michael Bilirakis</b> is an American lawyer and politician serving as the U.S. representative for Florida's 12th congressional district since 2013. A member of the Republican Party, he first entered Congress in 2007, where he succeeded his father Michael Bilirakis, representing Florida's 9th congressional district until redistricting. His district includes much of the northern portion of the Tampa Bay area. Bilirakis previously served as the Florida state representative for the 48th district from 1998 to 2006.</p>"}